#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:1
msgid "Cache Store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:3
msgid ""
"A Cache Store is responsible for storing and retrieving cached responses."
" It is also responsible for deciding which specific response to use based"
" off of a response's `Vary` header (if present). It is expected to be "
"compliant with [RFC-9111](https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc9111.html)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:8
msgid "Pre-built Cache Stores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:10
msgid "`MemoryCacheStore`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:12
msgid "The `MemoryCacheStore` stores the responses in-memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:14 ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:45
msgid "**Options**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:16
msgid ""
"`maxSize` - The maximum total size in bytes of all stored responses. "
"Default `104857600` (100MB)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:17
msgid "`maxCount` - The maximum amount of responses to store. Default `1024`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:18
msgid ""
"`maxEntrySize` - The maximum size in bytes that a response's body can be."
" If a response's body is greater than or equal to this, the response will"
" not be cached. Default `5242880` (5MB)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:20
msgid "Getters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:22
msgid "`MemoryCacheStore.size`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:24
msgid "Returns the current total size in bytes of all stored responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:26
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:28
msgid "`MemoryCacheStore.isFull()`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:30
msgid ""
"Returns a boolean indicating whether the cache has reached its maximum "
"size or count."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:32
msgid "Events"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:34
msgid "`'maxSizeExceeded'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:36
msgid ""
"Emitted when the cache exceeds its maximum size or count limits. The "
"event payload contains `size`, `maxSize`, `count`, and `maxCount` "
"properties."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:39
msgid "`SqliteCacheStore`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:41
msgid ""
"The `SqliteCacheStore` stores the responses in a SQLite database. Under "
"the hood, it uses Node.js' "
"[`node:sqlite`](https://nodejs.org/api/sqlite.html) api. The "
"`SqliteCacheStore` is only exposed if the `node:sqlite` api is present."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:47
msgid ""
"`location` - The location of the SQLite database to use. Default "
"`:memory:`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:48
msgid ""
"`maxCount` - The maximum number of entries to store in the database. "
"Default `Infinity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:49
msgid ""
"`maxEntrySize` - The maximum size in bytes that a response's body can be."
" If a response's body is greater than or equal to this, the response will"
" not be cached. Default `Infinity`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:51
msgid "Defining a Custom Cache Store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:53
msgid "The store must implement the following functions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:55
msgid "Getter: `isFull`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:57
msgid ""
"Optional. This tells the cache interceptor if the store is full or not. "
"If this is true, the cache interceptor will not attempt to cache the "
"response."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:60
msgid "Function: `get`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:62 ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:78
msgid "Parameters:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:64 ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:80
msgid "**req** `Dispatcher.RequestOptions` - Incoming request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:66
msgid ""
"Returns: `GetResult | Promise<GetResult | undefined> | undefined` - If "
"the request is cached, the cached response is returned. If the request's "
"method is anything other than HEAD, the response is also returned. If the"
" request isn't cached, `undefined` is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:69
msgid ""
"The `get` method may return a `Promise` for async cache stores (e.g. "
"Redis-backed or remote stores). The cache interceptor handles both "
"synchronous and asynchronous return values, including in revalidation "
"paths (304 Not Modified handling and stale-while-revalidate background "
"revalidation)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:71
msgid "Response properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:73
msgid "**response** `CacheValue` - The cached response data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:74
msgid ""
"**body** `Readable | Iterable<Buffer> | undefined` - The response's body."
" This can be an array of `Buffer` chunks (with a `.values()` method) or a"
" `Readable` stream. Both formats are supported in all code paths, "
"including 304 revalidation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:76
msgid "Function: `createWriteStream`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:81
msgid "**value** `CacheValue` - Response to store"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:83
msgid ""
"Returns: `Writable | undefined` - If the store is full, return "
"`undefined`. Otherwise, return a writable so that the cache interceptor "
"can stream the body and trailers to the store."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:85
msgid "`CacheValue`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:87
msgid ""
"This is an interface containing the majority of a response's data (minus "
"the body)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:89
msgid "Property `statusCode`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:91
msgid "`number` - The response's HTTP status code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:93
msgid "Property `statusMessage`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:95
msgid "`string` - The response's HTTP status message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:97
msgid "Property `rawHeaders`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:99
msgid "`Buffer[]` - The response's headers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:101
msgid "Property `vary`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/api_CacheStore.md:103
msgid ""
"`Record<string, string | string[] | null> | undefined` - The headers "
"defined by the response's `Vary` header and their respective values for "
"later comparison. Values are `null` when the header specified in `Vary` "
"was not present in the original request. These `null` values are "
"automatically filtered out during revalidation so they are not sent as "
"request headers."
msgstr ""

